# Order-To-Cash (.NET) — build-context excludes for every image built by
# docker-compose.apps.yml (phase 23). Build context for the six .NET service
# images and the web image is the REPO ROOT (project references and
# apps/web's own workspace both need more than one directory) — without this
# file that context would drag in ~1.4 GB of local bin/obj output, two
# node_modules trees, .git and every prior test run's artifacts on every
# single-line Dockerfile edit.
#
# Nothing here excludes a FILE a Dockerfile's own COPY instructions actually
# need — checked by building every image (see progress/impl_full_docker_compose.md).

# .NET build output — every image rebuilds these from source inside its own
# stage; the host's own bin/obj must never leak into a container (different
# RID/config, and it would defeat Docker's own layer caching regardless).
**/bin/
**/obj/
TestResults/
**/TestResults/

# Node — apps/web installs its own inside the image; the host's copy is
# ~646 MB and irrelevant (different platform/arch in general).
**/node_modules/
apps/web/.next/
apps/web/coverage/
apps/web/test-results/
apps/web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# VCS and editor/OS noise.
.git/
.vscode/
.idea/
**/.DS_Store

# Nothing under these ever needs to reach a build context: logs are runtime
# output, and infra/* config is bind-mounted by docker-compose.infra.yml, not
# copied into an image.
logs/
n8n/
